  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "be2c4668",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 2: Profile an anemoi model\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 The configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "The file `perf_profiling.yaml` is the configuration for all the runs in this notebook.\n",
    "It is a normal anemoi training configuration, with these changes:\n",
    "\n",
    "* It trains on **20 batches** only, with a batch size of 1. A run takes approximately 1 to 2 minutes.\n",
    "* It uses the ERA5 dataset on the O96 grid (approximately 1 degree) and a GraphTransformer model.\n",
    "* It switches on the **benchmark profiler** (`diagnostics.benchmark_profiler`).\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cell below to see the configuration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c80cc12e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(open(\"perf_profiling.yaml\").read())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f009fb6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Look at the `benchmark_profiler` section:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Setting | What it does |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `memory.enabled` | Records a **profiler trace** (a `*.pt.trace.json` file) for `steps` steps, after `warmup` steps. |\n",
    "| `snapshot.enabled` | Records a **memory snapshot** (`memory_snapshot.pickle`) for `steps` steps, after `warmup` steps. |\n",
    "| `time.enabled` | Writes a report of the time for each part of the training loop. |\n",
    "| `speed.enabled` | Writes a report of the throughput. |\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Note:** We record only 2 steps. A trace of many steps is a very large file, and the web viewers become slow.\n",
    "\n",
    "To start a profiling run from a terminal, you use the command `anemoi-training profile` (not `anemoi-training train`):\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "anemoi-training profile --config-name=perf_profiling\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "In this notebook, the helper function `ph.run_experiment()` runs this command for you.\n",
    "You give it a name and a list of configuration changes (\"overrides\")."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "82963205",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2 Run the baseline\n",
    "\n",
    "The **baseline** uses the default settings of anemoi:\n",
    "\n",
    "* `num_chunks: 4` in the encoder, the processor and the decoder\n",
    "* `gradient_checkpointing: True` in the encoder, the processor and the decoder\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cell below. It takes approximately 1 to 2 minutes. The first run can take longer, because it creates the graph.\n",
    "While you wait, read the log file `outputs/baseline/run.log`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "aa6eacc0-90b8-40e6-96d0-338ec8852d8e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
